cff-version: 1.2.0
title: nmap-detections
message: If you use these checks or the lab in your own work, please cite them.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shakel
    family-names: Ahmed
    affiliation: CyberDesserts
repository-code: https://github.com/cyberdesserts/nmap-detections
url: https://blog.cyberdesserts.com/
abstract: >-
  Detection-only Nmap NSE checks for newly disclosed vulnerabilities. Each
  check ships with a reproducible Docker lab holding a case for every state
  the check can report, and the recorded results of running it. The first
  check covers the nginx2root HTTP/2 flaws in NGINX Open Source,
  CVE-2026-123007 and CVE-2026-123633, and tests whether HTTP/2 is live on
  the port as well as reading the version banner.
keywords:
  - nmap
  - nse
  - vulnerability-detection
  - nginx
  - http2
  - cve-2026-123007
  - cve-2026-123633
license: MIT
